<title>USA: Proteon Inc Q4 net loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Proteon Inc Q4 net loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>WESTBORO, Mass. 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended Twelve months ended</p>
<p>				 Dec. 31, Dec. 31,  Dec. 31, Dec. 31,</p>
<p>					 1996    1995     1996     1995</p>
<p> Net sales			 10,043  17,228    45,296  75,323</p>
<p>  Restructure cost		3,312     ---     3,312     ---</p>
<p>   Total operating expenses  10,469   7,373    32,741  31,388</p>
<p> Net (loss) income	   ( 8,047)   1,571 ($12,014)   8,220</p>
<p>(Loss) income per common share</p>
<p>				    ( 0.52)    0.10   ( 0.77)    0.52</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>common and common equivalent</p>
<p>  shares outstanding	   15,560  15,806    15,630  15,692</p>
<p>				    (in thousands)</p>
<p>NOTE:  The company said the net loss for 1996 included a $3,312,000, or $0.21 per share, for restructuring charges. Excluding the restructuring charge, the loss from operations was $0.31 per share, which includes $0.16 per share from ongoing operations and $0.15 per share from an inventory reserve.</p>
